When I'm not playing Monks, I'll often bring a random weapon up to
basic, if it's the best thing I've found so far.  The beginning of the
game is the hardest part, so I like to make it as easy as possible.
Yes, it might make the end game a bit harder, but the end game would
still be way easier than the beginning of the game.

Due to luckstones, the only weapons I feel really need to be boosted
high are projectiles (if my class can multishot them), martial arts,
lances, and polearms.  I'll also generally only boost one weapon really
high per game.

Even when I'm a wizard, the only spell schools I feel really need to be
boosted high are attack and divination.

I also use rocks against water monsters, and many of my classes like to
hit monsters with dwarvish mattocks.



